{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence using memoization.\n    The sequence is defined by P(1)=1, P(2)=1, and P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n-P(n-1)) for n > 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    memo = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\n    def _calculate_recursive(k: int) -> int:\n        # Return memoized value if already computed\n        if k in memo:\n            return memo[k]\n\n        # Apply the Newman-Conway recurrence relation for k > 2\n        # P(k) = P(P(k-1)) + P(k-P(k-1))\n        \n        # First, compute P(k-1) which is needed for both terms\n        pk_minus_1 = _calculate_recursive(k - 1)\n        \n        # Compute the two terms recursively and sum them\n        result = _calculate_recursive(pk_minus_1) + _calculate_recursive(k - pk_minus_1)\n        \n        # Store the result in the memoization table before returning\n        memo[k] = result\n        return result\n\n    # The problem context implies `n` will be a valid positive integer (n >= 1).\n    # The sequence is undefined for n <= 0.\n    return _calculate_recursive(n)"}
