{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n, m):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Eulerian number A(n, m).\n    A(n, m) is the number of permutations of {1, ..., n} with exactly m ascents.\n    \"\"\"\n    if m < 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1 if m == 0 else 0\n    if m >= n:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize a DP table where dp[i][j] stores A(i, j).\n    # The table has (n+1) rows and n columns, as m ranges from 0 to n-1.\n    dp = [[0 for _ in range(n)] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case for the recurrence relation.\n    dp[0][0] = 1 \n\n    # Fill the DP table using the recurrence A(i, j) = (j + 1) * A(i-1, j) + (i - j) * A(i-1, j-1).\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(i): # m ranges from 0 to i-1 for A(i, j)\n            term2 = 0\n            if j - 1 >= 0:\n                term2 = dp[i-1][j-1]\n            term1 = dp[i-1][j]\n            \n            dp[i][j] = (j + 1) * term1 + (i - j) * term2\n\n    return dp[n][m]"}
